1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Suppose you train a classifier to distinguish penguins from camels.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
In your dataset, all penguins are on snow, and camels are on sand.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
The classes are perfectly separable.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The model easily achieves ninety-eight percent training accuracy. But look closely.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The decision boundary only aligns with the background color.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
It ignores the animal shape.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
So, when we place a penguin on sand, the model predicts camel.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The prediction is wrong. The model relied on a shortcut.
